\caption(Each pair shares starting kernels and batch order; selected parameter and state checkpoints restore into a fresh model.)
\alttext(Each pair shares starting kernels and batch order; selected parameter and state checkpoints restore into a fresh model.)


> Conclusion

The one-step state update matches its analytic moments. Paired fits expose Adam updates,
validation selection and separate moving statistics; inference is independent of batch companions
and checkpoint restoration reproduces logits. Small paired runs do not establish a universal BN advantage.

> References

- [Ioffe and Szegedy (2015), Batch Normalization](https://arxiv.org/abs/1502.03167).
- [LeCun et al. (1998), Gradient-Based Learning Applied to Document Recognition](https://doi.org/10.1109/5.726791).
- [MNIST dataset](https://yann.lecun.org/exdb/mnist/).
